From: Codex <codex@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] explorer: leave shell endpoints to the opt-in external shell

Purpose: prevent two shells owning public taskbar, DDE and shell browser endpoints.
XP behavior: explorer supplies its own Shell_TrayWnd, folder DDE server and
ShellWindows class factory. The builtin desktop manager currently creates a
second hidden Shell_TrayWnd and starts those endpoints despite patch 0003.
Window enumeration confirms both taskbars; native folder/app commands fail.
Disable the builtin endpoints with the same external-shell opt-in, while
retaining the Wine desktop manager's display and clipboard responsibilities.
This addresses an observed ownership conflict; folder launch needs retesting.
No Microsoft implementation code is used.

--- a/programs/explorer/desktop.c
+++ b/programs/explorer/desktop.c
@@ -1293,10 +1293,12 @@
         initialize_display_settings( width, height );
         initialize_appbar();
 
-        initialize_systray( using_root, enable_shell, show_systray, no_tray_items );
+        if (!GetEnvironmentVariableW( L"WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL", NULL, 0 ))
+            initialize_systray( using_root, enable_shell, show_systray, no_tray_items );
         if (!using_root && enable_launchers) initialize_launchers( hwnd );
 
-        if ((shell32 = LoadLibraryW( L"shell32.dll" )) &&
+        if (!GetEnvironmentVariableW( L"WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL", NULL, 0 )
+            && (shell32 = LoadLibraryW( L"shell32.dll" )) &&
             (pShellDDEInit = (void *)GetProcAddress( shell32, (LPCSTR)188)))
         {
             pShellDDEInit( TRUE );
@@ -1319,8 +1321,11 @@
         }
     }
 
-    desktopshellbrowserwindow_init();
-    shellwindows_init();
+    if (!GetEnvironmentVariableW( L"WIN4WINE_EXTERNAL_SHELL", NULL, 0 ))
+    {
+        desktopshellbrowserwindow_init();
+        shellwindows_init();
+    }
 
     /* Ideally we would set the window of an IShellView here, but we never
        actually create one, so the desktop window itself will have to do. */
